00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.463
Recently, researchers at McGill

00:01:37.496 --> 00:01:40.733
have embarked on a study that
uses a brain scanning device

00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:44.537
to read people's minds
and implant thoughts

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:48.374
into their heads, or so
their subjects think.

00:01:48.407 --> 00:01:49.575
Now the same device may be able

00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:52.345
to help kids with ADHD, anxiety,

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:53.579
Obsessive Compulsive Disorder,

00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:56.449
migraines, Tourette's, and more.

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:01.821
This study is not
about technology.

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:04.924
The MRI machine behind
me may look impressive,

00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:08.728 align:start size:97% position:3%
but it's a sham, it's
deactivated, non functioning.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:13.766
What this study is really
about is faith, in science.

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:16.603
It's about the power
of thoughts to heal.

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:27.246
All you need is the
power of suggestion.

00:02:27.279 --> 00:02:28.848
(machine humming)

00:02:28.881 --> 00:02:31.684
(upbeat music)

00:02:41.994 --> 00:02:44.964
A placebo is something
that shouldn't work,

00:02:44.997 --> 00:02:47.433 align:start size:81% position:19%
but due to the
power of suggestion,

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:50.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
and because of the strength
of our belief, does,

00:02:50.402 --> 00:02:53.639 align:start size:97% position:3%
but we don't fully
understand yet how they work,

00:02:53.672 --> 00:02:56.642 align:start size:91% position:9%
there could be an
evolutionary explanation.

00:02:56.675 --> 00:02:59.445
For example, if a small
child hurts themselves,

00:02:59.478 --> 00:03:03.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
negative symptoms like pain
and crying can be good.

00:03:03.382 --> 00:03:05.851 align:start size:81% position:19%
They keep the child
safe and still,

00:03:05.884 --> 00:03:08.254 align:start size:81% position:19%
while signaling
adults to come help.

00:03:08.287 --> 00:03:12.258
When help arrives, even if
it has no active effect.

00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:14.594
The child's brain may
feel it has permission

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:17.563
to redirect resources
away from seeking help,

00:03:17.596 --> 00:03:19.966
and on to actually healing.

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:21.667 align:start size:84% position:16%
Modern medicine has
found a way to harness

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:25.271 align:start size:84% position:16%
this power by
prescribing placebos.

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:27.573 align:start size:81% position:19%
But not all placebos
work the same.

00:03:27.606 --> 00:03:30.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
For example, a sugar pill
will help your headache more

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:34.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
if given to you by a doctor
than by a poker buddy,

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.617
and the color of the
placebo matters too.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.620
A blue pill will work
to make you feel calm,

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.321
better than a white pill,

00:03:42.354 --> 00:03:45.024
because blue is a
more calming color.

00:03:45.057 --> 00:03:47.660 align:start size:81% position:19%
And a red pill
will keep you awake

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:50.496
and give you more energy
than a blue pill will.

00:03:50.529 --> 00:03:53.399
A capsule will work
better than a pill

00:03:53.432 --> 00:03:55.535
because it looks more important.

