02:21:06.891 --> 02:21:08.559
- Yeah, yeah.

02:21:08.592 --> 02:21:10.862
- But how was, well I guess
we should even start with

02:21:10.895 --> 02:21:14.732 align:start position:0%
like an MRI, basically how
that works, and then diffusion.

02:21:14.765 --> 02:21:17.702 align:start size:81% position:19%
- So an MRI is using
magnetic fields

02:21:17.735 --> 02:21:21.906
to image various kinds of
molecules in your brain.

02:21:21.939 --> 02:21:23.875
And depending on the
scanning protocol,

02:21:23.908 --> 02:21:25.676 align:start size:78% position:22%
you can pick up
on different kinds

02:21:25.709 --> 02:21:27.979
of structures in your brain.

02:21:28.012 --> 02:21:30.648
And what diffusion MRI
specifically is doing

02:21:30.681 --> 02:21:33.951
is looking at the direction
of water flow in your brain.

02:21:33.984 --> 02:21:37.822 align:start size:91% position:9%
So if you look at a really
big white matter tract,

02:21:37.855 --> 02:21:40.291
so white matter is
the sort of big wires

02:21:40.324 --> 02:21:42.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
that bridge different areas
of our brains together.

02:21:42.660 --> 02:21:45.796 align:start size:84% position:16%
So you have a cortex,
actually, may I?

02:21:45.829 --> 02:21:47.832
- Please, yeah, visual aids.

02:21:48.999 --> 02:21:50.868 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So they actually don't
really show it here.

02:21:50.901 --> 02:21:54.639 align:start size:97% position:3%
But all this stuff on the
inside would be white matter.

02:21:54.672 --> 02:21:56.707
So it's like if I have
some area here that needs

02:21:56.740 --> 02:21:58.843
to send a signal to
some area over here,

02:21:58.876 --> 02:22:00.745 align:start size:84% position:16%
there's a large
basically white wire,

02:22:00.778 --> 02:22:03.281 align:start size:88% position:13%
- And it's a white
because it's myelinated.

02:22:03.314 --> 02:22:04.649 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Exactly.
- It's covered in fat.

02:22:04.682 --> 02:22:05.850
- Exactly, yeah.

02:22:05.883 --> 02:22:07.752 align:start size:81% position:19%
Which helps the
signal transaction.

02:22:07.785 --> 02:22:09.120
- So if this was a
real person's brain,

02:22:09.153 --> 02:22:11.222
we would we would see
a more white color

02:22:11.255 --> 02:22:12.924
on the inside than
we do on this model.

02:22:12.957 --> 02:22:15.560
- Yeah exactly, it would
literally be gray up here,

02:22:15.593 --> 02:22:16.727
and white on the inside.

02:22:16.760 --> 02:22:18.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Gray matter white matter.
- Yep.

02:22:18.228 --> 02:22:19.263
- And so diffusion MRIs

02:22:19.296 --> 02:22:22.199 align:start size:91% position:9%
